1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,499
Welcome to this demonstration for the owner of Ramashree Gurukul
Music Institute. We will explore every menu

2
00:00:06,499 --> 00:00:09,557
and connect each one to a business benefit.

3
00:00:10,267 --> 00:00:17,462
All students, payments and concerts shown here are fictional. These
are the actual app interface screens, captured

4
00:00:17,462 --> 00:00:21,694
in a browser preview, rather than on an Android phone.

5
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:28,923
Home gives the owner a quick view of active students, fee
collections, pending fees and event earnings.

6
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:35,938
Filter by month, course, trainer or student status to review a
specific part of the institute.

7
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:43,828
Upcoming classes, concerts and student journeys help you decide what
needs attention before the teaching day begins.

8
00:00:44,533 --> 00:00:53,735
Students brings enrolment status, assigned trainers, courses and
learning progress together. Search and status filters make follow-up

9
00:00:53,735 --> 00:00:54,276
easier.

10
00:00:54,933 --> 00:01:02,371
Open a student to review contact details, guardian information and
preferences. This gives your team context when

11
00:01:02,371 --> 00:01:04,121
speaking with a parent.

12
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:12,245
Learning progress and the session timeline show what has been
completed and what remains. This supports better

13
00:01:12,245 --> 00:01:14,872
progress discussions and continuity between classes.

14
00:01:15,533 --> 00:01:23,696
The enrolment form captures music interests, class preferences,
assigned trainer, work packets, fee terms and a learning

15
00:01:23,696 --> 00:01:24,176
goal.

16
00:01:24,867 --> 00:01:31,410
Keeping these details together can reduce repeated questions and
help the owner plan a suitable learning path.

17
00:01:32,067 --> 00:01:40,936
Sessions tracks planned, completed, missed, rescheduled and
cancelled classes. The planned filter helps identify the next
classes

18
00:01:40,936 --> 00:01:41,979
to deliver.

19
00:01:42,667 --> 00:01:50,338
Mark complete opens the class record with actual date and
attendance. Notes, feedback, assignments and the next

20
00:01:50,338 --> 00:01:52,594
action preserve the teaching context.

21
00:01:53,267 --> 00:02:00,781
Alternative dates and a reschedule reason help track changes. This
can improve class coordination and make delivered

22
00:02:00,781 --> 00:02:02,549
sessions easier to review.

23
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:11,336
Fees separates paid, part paid, pending and overdue plans. Each
record shows the amount collected and the

24
00:02:11,336 --> 00:02:12,293
remaining balance.

25
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:21,619
Filter overdue fees to focus collection follow-ups. Fee plans
support discounts and due dates, so agreed terms

26
00:02:21,619 --> 00:02:22,633
remain visible.

27
00:02:23,333 --> 00:02:29,441
Open a fee record to review payment receipts and the balance. This
can reduce uncertainty when a

28
00:02:29,441 --> 00:02:31,956
parent asks what has already been paid.

29
00:02:32,667 --> 00:02:38,705
Here we record a fictional five hundred rupee UPI payment with a
receipt number and a reference.

30
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:46,355
After saving, the balance and receipt history update. The app
records a payment made elsewhere; this version

31
00:02:46,355 --> 00:02:49,628
does not collect money through an online gateway.

32
00:02:50,333 --> 00:02:59,229
More opens six additional sections: People, Work packets, Concerts,
Reminders, Reports and Settings. We will visit each

33
00:02:59,229 --> 00:03:00,276
of them.

34
00:03:00,933 --> 00:03:08,863
People has separate tabs for trainers and artists. Trainers shows
expertise, available slots and the number of

35
00:03:08,863 --> 00:03:09,796
assigned students.

36
00:03:10,467 --> 00:03:18,057
A trainer profile includes workload and estimated commission.
Commission uses collections from currently assigned students, so the

37
00:03:18,057 --> 00:03:21,629
owner should review it before making a payout.

38
00:03:22,333 --> 00:03:29,136
The Artists tab keeps vocalists, instrumentalists, accompanists and
other performance roles together.

39
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:39,237
Profiles include expertise, availability, stage preferences and
expected payout. This helps shortlist talent and prepare a realistic

40
00:03:39,237 --> 00:03:40,347
event budget.

41
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:49,758
Work packets defines courses and packages with session counts and
fees. The sample includes vocal, guitar, keyboard

42
00:03:49,758 --> 00:03:51,303
and workshop offerings.

43
00:03:52,000 --> 00:04:00,279
A work packet can specify duration, prerequisites, batch size,
pricing type and special rules. Clear terms help

44
00:04:00,279 --> 00:04:03,687
staff explain the offer consistently at enrolment.

45
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:12,343
Concerts keeps program dates, venue, organizer and participating
artists, students and trainers in one record.

46
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:20,461
The financial view separates billed earnings from cash actually
received, and shows total costs and the organizer

47
00:04:20,461 --> 00:04:25,727
balance. This distinction helps the owner assess both profitability
and cash flow.

48
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:34,093
The expense ledger records sound, venue, travel, marketing and
artist payouts with dates and references.

49
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:40,543
Use Record expense or payout to capture each paid cost and link an
artist when relevant. The

50
00:04:40,543 --> 00:04:44,598
business benefit is a clearer view of where event revenue is going.

51
00:04:45,267 --> 00:04:52,987
Reminders gathers items due soon or needing attention. The Fee and
Class tabs help prioritise collection calls

52
00:04:52,987 --> 00:04:54,349
and upcoming lessons.

53
00:04:55,000 --> 00:05:00,083
The Assignment and Event tabs support learning follow-through and
program preparation.

54
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:08,278
Prepare message creates editable reminder text. In the Android app,
you choose a messaging app and confirm

55
00:05:08,278 --> 00:05:12,237
the recipient and delivery yourself; sending is not automatic.

56
00:05:12,933 --> 00:05:21,112
The Event tab surfaces upcoming programs. Combined with the other
reminder categories, it helps the owner maintain

57
00:05:21,112 --> 00:05:23,036
a practical follow-up routine.

58
00:05:23,733 --> 00:05:32,253
Reports includes seven views. Business summary brings key activity
and financial measures together, with a month filter

59
00:05:32,253 --> 00:05:33,756
for periodic reviews.

60
00:05:34,467 --> 00:05:42,184
Student progress compares completed sessions with the target and
remaining sessions. Use it to review learning delivery

61
00:05:42,184 --> 00:05:43,999
and guide parent conversations.

62
00:05:44,667 --> 00:05:53,755
Trainer workload shows assigned students, delivered and pending
sessions, collections and estimated commission. It supports capacity
planning

63
00:05:53,755 --> 00:05:55,359
and payout review.

64
00:05:56,067 --> 00:06:05,424
Fee balances consolidates charges, discounts, collections and
outstanding amounts. This gives the owner a structured list for

65
00:06:05,424 --> 00:06:06,524
collection follow-ups.

66
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:15,224
Course revenue groups financial activity by work packet. It helps
compare collections and balances across offerings when

67
00:06:15,224 --> 00:06:17,113
reviewing pricing and demand.

68
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:26,117
Event profitability compares revenue, costs, earnings and cash
surplus. Use it to review which programs are financially

69
00:06:26,117 --> 00:06:29,542
worthwhile and which organizer payments remain pending.

70
00:06:30,200 --> 00:06:39,952
Artist payouts summarises recorded payments to performers. This
supports payout reconciliation and conversations with participating
artists.

71
00:06:40,667 --> 00:06:47,267
Every report offers CSV export for Excel and Save as PDF. These help
share a review with

72
00:06:47,267 --> 00:06:49,984
an accountant or keep a periodic record.

73
00:06:50,667 --> 00:06:59,760
Settings includes institute naming, PIN changes, locking and local
account management. The Android app supports Owner, Admin,

74
00:06:59,760 --> 00:07:04,039
Trainer, Artist, Student or Parent, and Finance roles.

75
00:07:04,733 --> 00:07:11,466
Linked roles see their permitted records. Accounts belong to this
phone and do not provide remote access

76
00:07:11,466 --> 00:07:13,446
or synchronise with another device.

77
00:07:14,133 --> 00:07:22,985
The Android app stores records in an encrypted local file. Settings
offers password-protected backup and restore, including

78
00:07:22,985 --> 00:07:24,026
local accounts.

79
00:07:24,733 --> 00:07:31,470
You can also enable a local daily reminder summary. Android may
delay alerts to save battery. These

80
00:07:31,470 --> 00:07:37,810
phone features are shown here as interface options and were not
executed in this browser recording.

81
00:07:38,467 --> 00:07:46,077
Getting started lets the owner load or remove sample records. Remove
fictional data before adding real institute

82
00:07:46,077 --> 00:07:46,525
records.

83
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:53,701
Audit history records changes with the user and time. It gives the
owner a useful trail when

84
00:07:53,701 --> 00:07:54,848
reviewing what changed.

85
00:07:55,533 --> 00:08:03,653
For Ramashree Gurukul, the value is a connected view of students,
teaching delivery, collections and performances, with

86
00:08:03,653 --> 00:08:05,086
fewer scattered records.

87
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:14,474
The current app works offline on one Android device. Multi-device
synchronisation, online payments and automatic message delivery

88
00:08:14,474 --> 00:08:20,087
would require a future backend integration. This concludes the
owner’s walkthrough.
